 It's been a busy week. secr 4.3.1 (now on CRAN) has some significant bug fixes and a few new features <https://www.otago.ac.nz/density/secr%204.3.1%20NEWS.txt>. The first serious release of secrapp (a Shiny app for running secr) is now live <https://www.stats.otago.ac.nz/secrapp> (note also the step-by-step guide <https://www.otago.ac.nz/density/pdfs/secrapp-tutorial.html>). Changes in openCR 1.4.2 and 1.4.4 are minor <https://cran.r-project.org/package=openCR/NEWS>. The Density web page <https://www.otago.ac.nz/density> has been updated: it's time to push the old Windows application Density into the background. Raw input files <https://www.otago.ac.nz/density/examples/index.html> are provided there for various examples.

The live <https://www.stats.otago.ac.nz/secrapp> link lets you run secrapp on a University of Otago machine without installing it yourself. We will see how this works out: peaks in demand may crash it, so for class use etc. you will probably want to run it locally (see GitHub <https://github.com/MurrayEfford/secrapp>).

